sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant O as Orchestrator
    participant SQL as get_customer_outstanding
    participant RC as retrieve_from_chat (sub-agent)
    participant L as ProvenanceLedger
    participant FA as final_answer

    U->>O: "How much does Sharma actually owe, and is there a dispute?"
    O->>SQL: customer_search="Sharma"
    SQL-->>L: register {ref: sql:1, value: 420000, source: invoices row INV-2201}
    SQL-->>O: "outstanding=420000 [ref:sql:1]"

    O->>RC: query="Sharma dispute", tenant_id
    RC->>RC: search_messages("Sharma dispute") -> msg_001
    RC->>RC: resolve_entity("Sharma") -> CUST-0078 (already a known name, no LLM needed)
    RC-->>L: register {ref: chat:1, value: "80000 disputed", sender: Ramesh, ts: 14 May, source: msg_001}
    RC-->>O: structured claim, ref chat:1

    O->>FA: numbers=[{value:420000, ref:sql:1}], qualifier={disputed_amount:{value:80000, ref:chat:1}}
    FA->>L: does sql:1 == 420000? does chat:1 == "80000 disputed"? both yes
    FA-->>O: validated, answer allowed to return
    O->>U: "Sharma Fabrics owes Rs 4,20,000 per the ERP (INV-2201). A chat message from Ramesh on 14 May disputes Rs 80,000 of that, citing short supply - unverified, not yet reflected in the ERP."
